        <h2>The LA Consulate and Its Jurisdiction</h2>
        <p>If you live in California, Arizona, Nevada, Hawaii, New Mexico, Utah, or Colorado and want to apply for Spain's <a href="/digital-nomad-visa-spain/">Digital Nomad Visa (DNV)</a>, the <strong>Consulate General of Spain in Los Angeles</strong> is your designated point of application. Under Spanish consular rules, you must apply at the consulate whose territory covers your state of <em>legal residence</em> &mdash; not where you happen to be staying or working when you submit your application.</p>

        <div class="jurisdiction-card">
          <h3>States Covered by the LA Consulate</h3>
          <div class="state-chips">
            <span class="state-chip">California</span>
            <span class="state-chip">Arizona</span>
            <span class="state-chip">Nevada</span>
